  "findings": [],
  "assessment": [
    "Fixed and output-resolution history gathers require positive finite derived bilinear support inside prior viewport, covered finite nonnegative color, and compatible depth. Invalid zero-weight or incompatible neighbors no longer discard valid support; empty support remains current-only. Existing clamp/reactivity policies remain.",
    "Fixed history stays on its jittered grid with original motion/depth. The 64-byte copy uniform presents at p plus current pixel jitter. CPU projection and affine fixture expectations use the matching sign; unjittered overlays and upscale composite omit current jitter.",
    "Extra depth-only variants share current canonical/skinned geometry, placements, MASK texture/cutoff, mirror/cull state and an unjittered matrix. Only existing disposable scene depth is overwritten after opaque resolve and before current-only overlays; saved motion/depth and history color are untouched.",
    "Temporal and upscale activation imply an admitted motion draw outside pixel-camera bypass. Overlay work is conditional on actual excluded draws. Models pass counting includes the extra pass; timestamp implementation is unchanged.",
    "Retained live/staging ownership and history/jitter phase publication remain after queue submission. Extra 144-byte uniform CPU/GPU payload is conservatively charged by doubling fixed Frame allocation charge; enlarged draw/owner headers are included via size_of. No added image allocation or per-frame pipeline compilation.",
    "Four additional depth pipelines are bounded startup work. Default zero-jitter output, locks, manifests, admission/refusal and web feature contracts remain. Cooked copy binding and depth-entry artifacts plus MetalFX postbuffer union require separate explicit review/recook."
  ],
